#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046669} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553606} :activity/id #uuid "380fb825-5be1-580a-990c-bf11f8d48700" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049041 :topic/id #uuid "d56dd46d-c76b-5160-925e-c4ddd2d90833" :topic/math-academy-id 3354} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553606 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172287 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28f429c0-4106-53ea-9c7e-5a3e5c69557c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}({e}^{\\pi }-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362984} {:answer/id #uuid "0560e91f-841f-5133-b19f-414819f58310" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}(2{e}^{2\\pi }-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362985} {:answer/id #uuid "e6c2c04d-6401-5b56-9894-aeead7dbe986" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}{e}^{2\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362986} {:answer/id #uuid "bbc5fcaa-258a-5aeb-90ce-1bd2af6582b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}({e}^{2\\pi }+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362987} {:answer/id #uuid "a210ea76-975d-59a6-8399-df6d3b035510" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}({e}^{\\pi }-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362988}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362984} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b62b53e-864d-5c41-bf41-a59840c727e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362983}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f2b06f7c-408a-5dfe-b281-0fde1f80e146" :question/math-academy-id "q-123354" :question/problem "![](images/d3/d33f9b851125443ff738fa4c3aedcbeaf8a202d05caa06747e74262c0ae89bd9.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r={e}^{2\\theta }\\,$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r={e}^{2\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=2{e}^{2\\theta }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we evaluate our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{({e}^{2\\theta })}^{2}+{(2{e}^{2\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{e}^{4\\theta }+4{e}^{4\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{5{e}^{4\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{e}^{2\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}{e}^{2\\theta }{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}({e}^{\\pi }-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}({e}^{\\pi }-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "20042ad6-2b50-5151-ad49-bb4eef91cd09" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553632}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553607 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259536 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "336fa244-06f6-591f-8966-fdfd73c6a423" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{(\\pi +2)}^{1/2}-8}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257235} {:answer/id #uuid "58895e89-7919-506e-994d-1c2dbe196d4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{({\\pi }^{2}+4)}^{3/2}-8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257550} {:answer/id #uuid "c128e791-18c2-5301-8880-f7b4f01bfcb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{({\\pi }^{2}+4)}^{3/2}-4}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258470} {:answer/id #uuid "e274d3fe-784b-5699-8844-849e5934ed3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{(\\pi +2)}^{3/2}-8}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258753} {:answer/id #uuid "f808119a-e030-585c-82c2-c558a63e63a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{(\\pi +4)}^{1/2}-8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258958}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186257550} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4736e82-40af-567d-b32a-974a616d81a4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259346}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f5451ce0-d618-51ea-8499-28c757a17f08" :question/math-academy-id "q-123587" :question/problem "![](images/99/994b8cd2134d6d1e9a1e89559e462128c05fd5d3e7f4755c51931f3cf7f37268.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r={\\theta }^{2}\\,$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi ,$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r={\\theta }^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=2\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, we evaluate our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{({\\theta }^{2})}^{2}+{(2\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{\\theta }^{4}+4{\\theta }^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{\\theta }^{2}(4+{\\theta }^{2})}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\theta \\sqrt{4+{\\theta }^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }2\\theta \\sqrt{4+{\\theta }^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\frac{{(4+{\\theta }^{2})}^{3/2}}{3}|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{{({\\pi }^{2}+4)}^{3/2}-8}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "22e62c73-21df-5fda-9d79-ba9cdeb1a7a9" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553635}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553632 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400107 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04289a9d-17cf-573a-9701-d41c64ef2496" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}(5+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400109} {:answer/id #uuid "2cd6606e-b516-5f6f-9f4b-c6f100ea81db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{6-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400110} {:answer/id #uuid "41205926-9dd0-53e7-b1aa-ade02572e0a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{3+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400111} {:answer/id #uuid "be2d7cad-36f0-55ab-b08f-a68a53ffb570" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{5-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400112} {:answer/id #uuid "4933aa14-2d33-5b3a-973b-f6175f55c3af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{5+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400113}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400112} :answer-field/id #uuid "4bff7a0b-d96e-5598-95de-cbbd3ac2a012" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400108}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ffdfd696-312e-58bb-aa35-858898cb0c00" :question/math-academy-id "q-123519" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r=\\sqrt{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,$ for $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}$ ?" :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=\\sqrt{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{2\\sqrt{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expression for our line integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{(\\sqrt{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta })}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{2\\sqrt{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )+\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{4(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{\\frac{4(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(1-{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )}{4(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{\\frac{(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )(4-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{5-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "76362486-adbf-5459-b248-d212c1251f2c" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553652}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553635 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275248 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2dc039c6-5665-5166-aa53-9a15c6c4c91b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272795} {:answer/id #uuid "8b464717-8539-5469-8060-dac626a0833e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273588} {:answer/id #uuid "d4ea6766-0861-5a8d-8643-ea7eabf5bda5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274253} {:answer/id #uuid "d920ab5e-c0b5-5fd4-a193-1324a5a2e7cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274284} {:answer/id #uuid "e41b2b91-8816-5099-b2fa-6f471a4a0905" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274403}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272795} :answer-field/id #uuid "49db0e6a-b203-52c9-99a3-d2fa536b85d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274758}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4554a25e-9962-5d01-9655-91afa5f0b772" :question/math-academy-id "q-149815" :question/problem "![](images/62/624bb949d80c1da50cba951b00210a2a26aeb3c44d77d4c2eed69c8e3ba0f4d4.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{4},$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, we evaluate our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{{(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}^{2}+{(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{9{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +9{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{9}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =3\\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =3(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "7d0d777b-efed-57ba-b08b-6f64a58115f0"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553652 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447160 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d2aeb4a-6148-5344-8241-a30ca0414bf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}{csc}^{3}⁡\\theta \\sqrt{1+5{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447092} {:answer/id #uuid "369bbef4-e31e-5ef6-9afb-de7d3e21d28f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}{csc}^{3}⁡\\theta \\sqrt{1+9{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447101} {:answer/id #uuid "39da32fb-4fd3-56f4-8b48-27bfa06dac2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta \\sqrt{1+8{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447105} {:answer/id #uuid "7d101eaf-b053-5e48-a386-fa7d17ca7d49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta \\sqrt{5+4{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447114} {:answer/id #uuid "ba9bc000-67c4-53d2-b325-fa53d6ea89eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta \\sqrt{1+7{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447132}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447101} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8dcb75d-dac3-5c81-8f6e-1e4763779208" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447150}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "fb00dc0e-66fe-5382-b23d-00ac1fa661b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-123559" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r={csc}^{3}⁡\\theta \\,$ for $\\pi /3\\le \\theta \\le \\pi /2?$" :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r={csc}^{3}⁡\\theta \\,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=-3{csc}^{3}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expression for our line integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{({csc}^{3}⁡\\theta )}^{2}+{(-3{csc}^{3}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{csc}^{6}⁡\\theta +9{csc}^{6}⁡\\theta {cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{csc}^{6}⁡\\theta (1+9{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta })\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}{csc}^{3}⁡\\theta \\sqrt{1+9{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "952b8495-fb82-537a-8ec9-22ad3d4e7fad" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553607}}] :activity/title "Further Properties of Line Integrals of Scalar Functions" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552854}]}
